<mxCell id="semantic_model-legend" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read it&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Orange: fact tables, with their measures. Blue: dimension tables. Green: the date table. Grey: other tables. A dashed box has no key.&lt;br&gt;A line is a relationship from the many side (crow's foot) to the one side: solid is active, dashed grey is inactive, dotted red is one the plan found that a tabular model cannot express as the tables stand." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="568" width="900" height="97" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="semantic_model-notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_vbap.MANDT+VBELN -&amp;gt; sap_vbak.MANDT+VBELN: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 2; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + VBELN) to `sap_vbak` and the matching column to `sap_vbap` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_vbep.MANDT+VBELN+POSNR -&amp;gt; sap_vbap.MANDT+VBELN+POSNR: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 3; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + VBELN + '|' + POSNR) to `sap_vbap` and the matching column to `sap_vbep` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_vbak.MANDT+KUNNR -&amp;gt; sap_kna1.MANDT+KUNNR: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 2; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + KUNNR) to `sap_kna1` and the matching column to `sap_vbak` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_vbak.MANDT+VKORG -&amp;gt; sap_tvko.MANDT+VKORG: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 2; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + VKORG) to `sap_tvko` and the matching column to `sap_vbak` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_vbap.MANDT+MATNR -&amp;gt; sap_mara.MANDT+MATNR: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 2; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + MATNR) to `sap_mara` and the matching column to `sap_vbap` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_makt.MANDT+MATNR -&amp;gt; sap_mara.MANDT+MATNR: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 2; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + MATNR) to `sap_mara` and the matching column to `sap_makt` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_tvko.MANDT+BUKRS -&amp;gt; sap_t001.MANDT+BUKRS: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 2; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + BUKRS) to `sap_t001` and the matching column to `sap_tvko` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_lips.MANDT+VBELN -&amp;gt; sap_likp.MANDT+VBELN: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 2; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + VBELN) to `sap_likp` and the matching column to `sap_lips` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_lips.MANDT+VGBEL+VGPOS -&amp;gt; sap_vbap.MANDT+VBELN+POSNR: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 3; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + VBELN + '|' + POSNR) to `sap_vbap` and the matching column to `sap_lips` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_lips.MANDT+MATNR -&amp;gt; sap_mara.MANDT+MATNR: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 2; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + MATNR) to `sap_mara` and the matching column to `sap_lips` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_likp.MANDT+KUNNR -&amp;gt; sap_kna1.MANDT+KUNNR: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 2; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + KUNNR) to `sap_kna1` and the matching column to `sap_likp` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;Not in the model: sap_likp.MANDT+KUNAG -&amp;gt; sap_kna1.MANDT+KUNNR: a tabular relationship uses one column per side, and this one needs 2; Direct Lake allows no calculated column to combine them. Add a combined key column (MANDT + '|' + KUNNR) to `sap_kna1` and the matching column to `sap_likp` in the lakehouse, for example in a gold view (gold_views_draft / create_gold_views), and relate on it.&lt;br&gt;And 12 more: hover over an arrow to read its reason." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="681" width="900" height="862" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
